# The design record is byte-normative: C1 of tools/checkers/design_record_consistency.py
# asserts zero CRLF pairs across the record documents, and the Phase 1 round-trip check
# compares generated documents to their committed form byte for byte. The developer
# machine has core.autocrlf=true set system-wide, which would rewrite LF to CRLF on
# checkout and turn both red. These rules override it for every file in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary forms that must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Evidence artifacts are DIGESTED in their manifest. Line-ending translation would
# change their bytes and the recorded sha256 would stop verifying on a fresh clone --
# measured: a captured runner transcript hashed 634ec09d in the working copy and
# 43b38324 as git would check it out. The digest exists to bind what the gate reads to
# what the demonstration produced, so these bytes are never touched.
verification/evidence/** -text
